    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14165",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $g$ defined by the mapping diagram shown below? \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193754/assets/5e01cbf87af705346d112ed8f65a40936f7bc38776146b2c98736a4712828389.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $g(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a mapping diagram, the range consists of all the outputs to which an arrow is drawn.\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{ 3,6,9,12 \\}.$",
